.\" Man page for ax25netd_agwpe_shadow.conf
.\"
.TH AX25NETD_AGWPE_SHADOW.CONF 5 "29 Sep 2026" "ax25-apps" "Linux System Administration"
.SH NAME
ax25netd_agwpe_shadow.conf \- credentials for ax25netd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ax25netd_agwpe_shadow.conf
holds the AGWPE login credentials used by
.BR ax25netd (8).
It lives next to
.BR ax25netd_agwpe.conf (5)
and must be readable only by root and the account ax25netd runs under
(mode 0600, owned by root).
.PP
Each line defines one credential:
.PP
.RS
.I target user password
.RE
.PP
Two kinds of targets exist:
.PP
.TP
.B ax25netd
General client authentication of this instance.  When
.B auth
is enabled in
.BR ax25netd_agwpe.conf (5),
every AGWPE client connecting to the loop port must present one of these
credentials before any other frame is accepted.  This covers local
applications as well as peer ax25netd boxes connecting in a chain
.RB ( see
.BR ax25netd (8)).
.TP
.I name
Optional login for the upstream of that name, sent by ax25netd to the
upstream after connecting.  Only needed when the upstream itself requires
a login, e.g. AGWPE on Windows or a second ax25netd in a chain.  Servers
without login support such as Direwolf need no entry and receive no
credentials.
.PP
A target that matches neither the reserved name nor any configured upstream
is a fatal configuration error; a missing file is not.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
	ax25netd	dl9sau	IforgotToChangeThisSecret
	master		dl9sau	IforgotToChangeThisSecret
.fi
.SH FILES
.I @@@AX25_SYSCONFDIR@@@/ax25netd_agwpe_shadow.conf
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ax25netd (8),
.BR ax25netd_agwpe.conf (5)
